Chapter: VecMaskHazards
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe for the mask query builtins, and the pin for the
 movmskpd REX omission.

 movmskpd was encoded with no REX byte, so a destination in R8-R15 lost
 its high bit and encoded the low-three-bits register instead. alloc-temp
 rotates [RAX, RCX, RDX, RSI, RDI, R11] and R11 is the only extended
 register in that pool, so a mask query whose temp landed there wrote its
 bits to RBX while the test-rr that follows read R11, and sete answered
 from whatever R11 held.

 Two things are needed to reach it, and every existing vector test in the
 tree has neither. The operands must have DISTINCT LANES, because
 vec-splat writes the same value to both and movmskpd can then only answer
 0 or 3 -- under which mask-any and mask-all are the same function and
 mask-count is never asked for 1. And several queries must sit in ONE
 arithmetic expression, because which temp a query is handed depends on
 how many the surrounding expression has already consumed. mk2 builds a
 distinct-lane vector by writing two doubles into a buffer, which is the
 only way to express one.

 The lane-uniform variants are the controls: they answer correctly even on
 a compiler carrying the defect, which is precisely why splat-only tests
 could not see it.

 This is a WITNESS rather than a guarantee. It reaches R11 through the
 temp rotation, and a future codegen change that shifts the rotation could
 stop reaching it while leaving the encoder wrong. If this test is ever
 suspected of having gone quiet, re-derive it by dumping the emitted bytes
 and checking that every movmskpd names the same register as the test-rr
 that follows it.

Section: Build

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (t) = if t then 1 else 0

  poke-bits : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  poke-bits (base) (off) (bits) (i) =
   if i >= 8 then 0
   else let b = bit-and (bit-shru bits (i * 8)) 255
   in let w = poke-byte base (off + i) b
   in poke-bits base off bits (i + 1)

  mk2 : Real, Real -> Vector 2 Real
  mk2 (x) (y) =
   let base = alloc-bytes 16
   in let a = poke-bits base 0 (real-to-bits x) 0
   in let b = poke-bits base 8 (real-to-bits y) 0
   in vec-load-at base

Section: Operands

  p1 : Real
  p1 = 1.0

  n2 : Real
  n2 = -2.0

  p20 : Real
  p20 = 20.0

  p10 : Real
  p10 = 10.0

  p2 : Real
  p2 = 2.0

Section: Probes

 An empty mask: every lane clear, so none is True and any and all are
 False.

 The operands arrive as PARAMETERS, not as chapter constants. A top-level
 constant is a zero-argument function and so a call, which consumes a
 different number of temps and moves the rotation; written against
 constants these same probes answer correctly on a compiler carrying the
 defect. Four parameters also fill the local registers, so the queries
 allocate against a spilled frame.

  empty-mixed : Real, Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  empty-mixed (x0) (x1) (y0) (y1) =
   let v = mk2 x0 x1
   in let w = mk2 y0 y1
   in let m = v < w
   in b2i (mask-any m) + 2 * b2i (mask-all m) + 4 * b2i (mask-none m)

  empty-same : Real, Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  empty-same (x0) (x1) (y0) (y1) =
   let v = mk2 x0 x1
   in let w = mk2 y0 y1
   in let m = v < w
   in b2i (mask-none m) + 2 * b2i (mask-none m) + 4 * b2i (mask-none m)

 A mixed mask: lane zero set, lane one clear. This is the pattern
 vec-splat cannot produce, and the only one under which count is 1.

  mixed-all-four : Real, Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  mixed-all-four (x0) (x1) (y0) (y1) =
   let v = mk2 x0 x1
   in let w = mk2 y0 y1
   in let m = v < w
   in b2i (mask-any m) + 2 * b2i (mask-all m) + 4 * b2i (mask-none m) + 8 * mask-count m

  mixed-count : Real, Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  mixed-count (x0) (x1) (y0) (y1) =
   let v = mk2 x0 x1
   in let w = mk2 y0 y1
   in let m = v < w
   in mask-count m + 2 * mask-count m + 4 * mask-count m

Section: Controls

 Lane-uniform operands. These answer correctly with or without the fix,
 so a run where these pass and the probes above fail is the signature of
 the defect rather than of vectors being broken generally.

  splat-empty : Real, Real -> Integer
  splat-empty (x) (y) =
   let v = vec-splat x
   in let w = vec-splat y
   in let m = v < w
   in b2i (mask-any m) + 2 * b2i (mask-all m) + 4 * b2i (mask-none m)

  splat-full : Real, Real -> Integer
  splat-full (x) (y) =
   let v = vec-splat x
   in let w = vec-splat y
   in let m = v < w
   in b2i (mask-any m) + 2 * b2i (mask-all m) + 4 * b2i (mask-none m) + 8 * mask-count m

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("empty-mixed: " & show (empty-mixed p1 n2 p1 n2))
   print-line-uni ("empty-same: " & show (empty-same p1 n2 p1 n2))
   print-line-uni ("mixed-all-four: " & show (mixed-all-four p1 p20 p10 p2))
   print-line-uni ("mixed-count: " & show (mixed-count p1 p20 p10 p2))
   print-line-uni ("splat-empty: " & show (splat-empty p1 p1))
   print-line-uni ("splat-full: " & show (splat-full p1 p20))
  end
